      "answer": "$v_C=\\sqrt5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ or $2.24\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$0.2\\times10\\times0.5=\\frac12\\times0.2\\times v_B^2$. M1 (Attempt PE or KE for motion from $A$ to $B$.)\n\nM1 (Attempt PE loss balances KE gain from $A$ to $B$.)\n\n$v_B^2=10$. A1\n\nAlternative method for the first 3 marks: $0.2\\times10\\times\\sin30^\\circ=0.2a$, $a=5$. (M1, attempt to find acceleration for motion from $A$ to $B$.) $v_B^2=0+2\\times5\\times1$. (M1, use $v^2=u^2+2as$.) $v_B^2=10$. (A1.)\n\nThen, either this method for the next 5 marks:\n\n$R=0.2\\times10\\times\\cos30^\\circ=\\sqrt3$. B1\n\n$F=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\times0.2\\times10\\times\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}=1.5$. M1 (For using $F=\\mu R$ where $R$ must be a component of $0.2g$.)\n\nPE loss $=0.2\\times10\\times0.5=1$; WD against $F=1.5\\times1$. M1 (Attempt to find either PE loss or WD against $F$ from $B$ to $C$.)\n\n$\\frac12\\times0.2\\times10+0.2\\times10\\times0.5=1.5\\times1+\\frac12\\times0.2\\times v_C^2$. M1 (Apply work-energy equation for motion from $B$ to $C$ as KE and PE at $B$ balance work done against $F$ and KE at $C$, with $v_B$ not equal to 0.)\n\n$v_C=\\sqrt5=2.24$ m s$^{-1}$. A1\n\nOR, for the next 5 marks: $R=\\sqrt3$ (B1); $F=1.5$ (M1, same $F=\\mu R$ guidance); $0.2\\times10\\sin30^\\circ-1.5=0.2a$, $a=-2.5$ (M1, attempt acceleration from $B$ to $C$); $v_C^2=10+2\\times(-2.5)\\times1$ (M1, use $v^2=u^2+2as$ with $v_B$ not equal to 0); $v_C=\\sqrt5=2.24$ m s$^{-1}$ (A1).\n\nAlternative method for question 7(a): PE loss $=0.2\\times10\\times2\\sin30^\\circ=2$ (M1); KE gain $=\\frac12\\times0.2\\times v_C^2$ (M1); both PE loss and KE gain correct (A1); $R=\\sqrt3$ (B1); $F=1.5$ (M1, same $F=\\mu R$ guidance); WD against $F=1.5\\times1$ (M1); $0.2\\times10\\times1=1.5\\times1+\\frac12\\times0.2\\times v_C^2$ (M1, attempt work-energy equation from $A$ to $C$); $v_C=\\sqrt5=2.24$ m s$^{-1}$ (A1).\n\nTotal: 8",
